    "threat_description": "VS Code autorun dropper. Payload in .vscode/tasks.json.\nOutbound: fetch-and-run. It downloads code from isvalid-regions.vercel.app and executes it (.vscode/tasks.json).\nRuns automatically when the folder is opened in VS Code (hidden folderOpen task that fetches and runs a remote script).\nMatches PolinRider / Contagious Interview (DPRK): fake-recruiter coding tasks that run a downloader when opened in VS Code. Payload host: isvalid-regions.vercel.app.\nCampaign GW-C-498a0aeb: one of 86 confirmed repos across 58 accounts sharing the dropper URL shape settings/{os}?flag=. Payload served from 18 distinct hosts, including 260120.vercel.app, default-configuration-sandy.vercel.app, default-configuration.vercel.app, isvalid-regions.vercel.app, vscode-bootstrapper.vercel.app.\nAttribution: the tradecraft is consistent with North Korea, but a single signal is a lead rather than an attribution, so we do not attribute it on this evidence alone. Signals: Delivery vector matches Contagious-Interview tradecraft: vscode-folderopen-autorun, dprk-dropper-path-shape.\nFound by GitHub code search for a confirmed malware signature: settings/linux?flag=; settings/mac?flag=; settings/windows?flag=.\nConfirmed by static analysis; the code was read, never executed.",
